# Bad / fake / OEM DMI values for glpi-additional-oem
#
# Supported formats:
#   value                 -> bad value for any field
#   field=value           -> bad value only for a specific DMI field
#   /regex/               -> bad regex for any field, matched after lowercasing
#   field:/regex/         -> bad regex only for a specific DMI field
#
# Known DMI fields used by the script:
#   sys_vendor
#   product_name
#   product_serial
#   product_uuid
#   board_vendor
#   board_name
#   board_serial
#
# Built-in bad values already include:
#   OEM, Default string, To be filled by O.E.M., System Serial Number,
#   Base Board Serial Number, None, Unknown, Not specified, Not available,
#   N/A, NA, NULL, all-zero strings, all-f strings.
#
# Add site-specific values below.

# Generic bad OEM placeholders
Default string
To be filled by O.E.M.
To be filled by OEM
System Serial Number
Base Board Serial Number
Chassis Serial Number
No Asset Information
Not Specified
Not Available
Unknown
None
N/A
NA
NULL
OEM

# Field-specific examples
product_serial=Default string
board_serial=Default string
product_name=Default string

# Regex examples
/^0+$/
/^f+$/
product_serial:/^serial number$/
board_serial:/^base board serial number$/
